  "issue_date": "2023-12-08",
  "report_week": "49",
  "report_period": "Week 49 (1st Dec to 8th Dec 2023)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Bocimar have committed their Capesize \"Mineral Ningbo\" 178/2009 SWS, China (SS/DD 07/2024) to Chinese buyers Agricore at region USD 20 mill. Remind you that back in July, the sister vessel \"Aquaproud\" 178/2009 SWS, China (SS/DD 06/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 18,9 mill. Furthermore, the \"The Mothership\" 177/2006 Mitsui, Japan (SS 03/2026, DD 05/2024, BWTS fitted) of Kassian Maritime was sold to Chinese interests at USD 17,4 mill. For comparison, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Satori\" 177/2007 Mitsui, Japan (SS 01/2026, DD 01/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a month ago at USD 18,5 mill. The Kamsarmax \"IC Harvest\" 83/2010 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 02/2024) was committed to Chinese interests for USD 17 mill, while the one-year-older \"Cymona Galaxy\" 81/2009 Universal, Japan (SS/DD 06/2024, BWTS fitted) from Alassia Newships Management was sold to Greek interests at high USD 15 mill basis delivery March 2024. Note that the \"ASL Neptune\" 82/2009 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 04/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a month ago at USD 16,2 mill. Navios Maritime have sold their Panamax \"Navios Hyperion\" 75/2004 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 02/2024) to Far Eastern interests at USD 9 mill. Remind you that the sister vessel \"HC Pioneer\" 75/2004 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 05/2024) was sold a couple of months ago at high USD 8 mill. On the Supramax sector, Byzantine Maritime sold their \"Ermione\" 56/2008 IHI, Japan (SS 09/2028, DD 06/2026, BWTS fitted) to Chinese buyers for USD 14,2 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Wave Runner\" 56/2008 IHI, Japan (SS/DD 04/2025) was sold back in September at high USD 12 mill. Suisse-Atlantique have sold their Handysize \"Vully\" 35/2011 Shinan, Korea (SS 06/2026, DD 06/2024, BWTS fitted) to Chinese interests at region USD 13 mill. Note that a week ago, the one-year-younger \"Navios Lyra\" 34/2012 Spp, Korea (SS 06/2027, DD 11/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 13,75 mill.",
    "tankers": "The Aframax \"S-Treasure\" 106/2005 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS/DD 09/2025, BWTS fitted) of Stalwart Management was sold to undisclosed buyers at USD 32 mill. Remind you that back in September, the scrubber fitted \"Wonder Vega\" 106/2005 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold at high USD 31 mill. The MR2 sister vessels \"Nord Sustainable\" & \"Nord Supreme\" 49/2015 Stx, Korea (SS/DD 05/2025 & SS/DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) were committed to Greek buyers for USD 39 mill each. Note that the two-years-older \"Nord Steady\" 50/2013 Stx, Korea (SS 06/2028, DD 06/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold back in October at USD 34,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of mid usd 12,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 14,000/16,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were fixed around usd 17,000/19,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 18,000/19,000 pd. Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 19,000/22,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into India were reported at the level of usd 38,000 pd. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed at the level of usd 16,000 pd for 19/21 months employment basis delivery China. Also, a Kamsarmax was fixed on period at the usd 18,500 pd basis delivery East Coast India for 5/7 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were fixed around usd 12,000/15,000 pd. Indonesian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Indian trips into China were fixed around usd 15,000/18,000 pd. West Coast Indian trips into East Coast India were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into US East Coast were fixed around usd 18,000 pd. An Ultramax was fixed on period at the usd 16,000 pd basis delivery China for 5/7 months employment.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of trips from Japan into South East Asia were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Trips from Black Sea via Mediterranean into US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. North Coast South American trips into East Coast South America were fixed around usd 19,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
